{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "defenseclaw_version": "0.5.0",
  "runtime_lock_file": "hook_contract_lock.json",
  "description": "DefenseClaw hook connector compatibility contracts. Each hook connector maps agent CLI version ranges to the hook script contract DefenseClaw knows how to install, decode, evaluate, and respond to.",
  "connectors": {
    "openclaw": {
      "kind": "proxy",
      "compatibility_gate": "not-gated",
      "version_probe": "openclaw --version",
      "contracts": [],
      "notes": [
        "OpenClaw is proxy-backed; hook contract pinning does not gate setup."
      ]
    },
    "zeptoclaw": {
      "kind": "proxy",
      "compatibility_gate": "not-gated",
      "version_probe": "zeptoclaw --version",
      "contracts": [],
      "notes": [
        "ZeptoClaw is proxy-backed; hook contract pinning does not gate setup."
      ]
    },
    "codex": {
      "kind": "hook",
      "compatibility_gate": "hook-contract",
      "version_probe": "codex --version",
      "contracts": [
        {
          "contract_id": "codex-hooks-v1",
          "agent_version": {
            "min_inclusive": "0.124.0",
            "max_exclusive": "0.129.0"
          },
          "default_for_unversioned": false,
          "hook_script_version": "v6",
          "hook_script": "codex-hook.sh",
          "hook_config_path_templates": [
            "~/.codex/config.toml",
            "~/.codex/managed_config.toml"
          ],
          "response_field": "codex_output",
          "events": [
            "SessionStart",
            "UserPromptSubmit",
            "PreToolUse",
            "PermissionRequest",
            "PostToolUse",
            "Stop"
          ],
          "aid_surfaces": [
            "prompt",
            "tool_call",
            "tool_result"
          ],
          "supports_traceparent": true,
          "native_otlp": true,
          "capabilities": {
            "can_block": true,
            "can_ask_native": false,
            "ask_events": [],
            "block_events": [
              "UserPromptSubmit",
              "PreToolUse",
              "PermissionRequest",
              "PostToolUse",
              "Stop"
            ],
            "supports_fail_closed": true,
            "scope": "user"
          },
          "notes": [
            "Codex 0.124.0 through 0.128.x expose six stable hook events. They have no hooks/list trust introspection and ignore hooks.state; validate them only as legacy no-bypass execution.",
            "DefenseClaw may preseed inert hook state for upgrade continuity, but does not describe 0.124.0 through 0.128.x as trust-certified.",
            "Codex has no native hook-side ask surface in this contract; confirm verdicts render as alert/systemMessage."
          ]
        },
        {
          "contract_id": "codex-hooks-v2",
          "agent_version": {
            "min_inclusive": "0.129.0",
            "max_exclusive": "0.133.0"
          },
          "default_for_unversioned": false,
          "hook_script_version": "v6",
          "hook_script": "codex-hook.sh",
          "hook_config_path_templates": [
            "~/.codex/config.toml",
            "~/.codex/managed_config.toml"
          ],
          "response_field": "codex_output",
          "events": [
            "SessionStart",
            "UserPromptSubmit",
            "PreToolUse",
            "PermissionRequest",
            "PostToolUse",
            "PreCompact",
            "PostCompact",
            "Stop"
          ],
          "aid_surfaces": [
            "prompt",
            "tool_call",
            "tool_result"
          ],
          "supports_traceparent": true,
          "native_otlp": true,
          "capabilities": {
            "can_block": true,
            "can_ask_native": false,
            "ask_events": [],
            "block_events": [
              "UserPromptSubmit",
              "PreToolUse",
              "PermissionRequest",
              "PostToolUse",
              "Stop"
            ],
            "supports_fail_closed": true,
            "scope": "user"
          },
          "notes": [
            "Codex 0.129.x through 0.132.x add PreCompact and PostCompact plus hooks/list trust introspection, for eight supported events.",
            "On native Windows the generic and command_windows values must remain byte-identical so 0.129.x and newer clients derive the same trusted hook identity.",
            "Codex has no native hook-side ask surface in this contract; confirm verdicts render as alert/systemMessage."
          ]
        },
        {
          "contract_id": "codex-hooks-v3",
          "agent_version": {
            "min_inclusive": "0.133.0",
            "max_exclusive": "0.145.0"
          },
          "default_for_unversioned": false,
          "hook_script_version": "v6",
          "hook_script": "codex-hook.sh",
          "hook_config_path_templates": [
            "~/.codex/config.toml",
            "~/.codex/managed_config.toml"
          ],
          "response_field": "codex_output",
          "events": [
            "SessionStart",
            "UserPromptSubmit",
            "PreToolUse",
            "PermissionRequest",
            "PostToolUse",
            "SubagentStart",
            "SubagentStop",
            "PreCompact",
            "PostCompact",
            "Stop"
          ],
          "aid_surfaces": [
            "prompt",
            "tool_call",
            "tool_result"
          ],
          "supports_traceparent": true,
          "native_otlp": true,
          "native_otlp_auth": "header-token",
          "native_otlp_signals": [
            "logs",
            "metrics",
            "traces"
          ],
          "native_otlp_endpoint_template": "/v1/<signal>",
          "capabilities": {
            "can_block": true,
            "can_ask_native": false,
            "ask_events": [],
            "block_events": [
              "SessionStart",
              "UserPromptSubmit",
              "PreToolUse",
              "PermissionRequest",
              "PostToolUse",
              "SubagentStop",
              "PreCompact",
              "PostCompact",
              "Stop"
            ],
            "supports_fail_closed": true,
            "scope": "user"
          },
          "notes": [
            "Codex 0.133.0 through 0.144.x expose the versioned ten-event DefenseClaw matrix, adding SubagentStart and SubagentStop.",
            "SessionStart, PreCompact, and PostCompact blocks render continue=false to stop the current turn, stop before compaction, or stop after compaction respectively. SubagentStop blocks render decision=block to continue the subagent flow.",
            "Stop decision=block continues Codex with a new continuation prompt. PostToolUse block cannot undo the completed tool side effect; its feedback replaces the result flow and rejects the tool promise in code mode.",
            "Release certification requires authentic packaged plus official-client evidence that hooks/list reports every owned handler enabled and trusted without a manual approval step; no such Windows record is attached, so this contract remains preview.",
            "Codex has no native hook-side ask surface in this contract; confirm verdicts render as alert/systemMessage."
          ]
        },
        {
          "contract_id": "codex-hooks-v4",
          "agent_version": {
            "min_inclusive": "0.145.0",
            "max_exclusive": ""
          },
          "default_for_unversioned": true,
          "hook_script_version": "v6",
          "hook_script": "codex-hook.sh",
          "hook_config_path_templates": [
            "~/.codex/config.toml",
            "~/.codex/managed_config.toml"
          ],
          "response_field": "codex_output",
          "events": [
            "SessionStart",
            "UserPromptSubmit",
            "PreToolUse",
            "PermissionRequest",
            "PostToolUse",
            "SubagentStart",
            "SubagentStop",
            "PreCompact",
            "PostCompact",
            "Stop",
            "SessionEnd"
          ],
          "aid_surfaces": [
            "prompt",
            "tool_call",
            "tool_result"
          ],
          "supports_traceparent": true,
          "native_otlp": true,
          "native_otlp_auth": "header-token",
          "native_otlp_signals": [
            "logs",
            "metrics",
            "traces"
          ],
          "native_otlp_endpoint_template": "/v1/<signal>",
          "capabilities": {
            "can_block": true,
            "can_ask_native": false,
            "ask_events": [],
            "block_events": [
              "SessionStart",
              "UserPromptSubmit",
              "PreToolUse",
              "PermissionRequest",
              "PostToolUse",
              "SubagentStop",
              "PreCompact",
              "PostCompact",
              "Stop"
            ],
            "supports_fail_closed": true,
            "scope": "user"
          },
          "notes": [
            "Codex 0.145.0 adds SessionEnd to the ten-event 0.133.0 through 0.144.x matrix.",
            "SessionEnd is a best-effort observation and telemetry event; it is not a block or native ask surface.",
            "SessionStart, PreCompact, and PostCompact blocks render continue=false to stop the current turn, stop before compaction, or stop after compaction respectively. SubagentStop blocks render decision=block to continue the subagent flow.",
            "Stop decision=block continues Codex with a new continuation prompt. PostToolUse block cannot undo the completed tool side effect; its feedback replaces the result flow and rejects the tool promise in code mode.",
            "Release certification requires authentic packaged plus official-client evidence that hooks/list reports every owned handler enabled and trusted without a manual approval step; no such Windows record is attached, so this contract remains preview.",
            "Codex has no native hook-side ask surface in this contract; confirm verdicts render as alert/systemMessage."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
