          "notes": [
            "opencode auto-loads JS/TS plugins from ~/.config/opencode/plugins/ — no command-hook config file to patch. DefenseClaw writes a dependency-free bridge plugin (defenseclaw.js) whose tool.execute.before POSTs to /api/v1/opencode/hook and throws on a block decision, aborting the tool.",
            "Block is the only active verdict; tool.execute.after is observe-only. The bridge honors fail-closed by throwing when the gateway is unreachable and FAIL_MODE=closed.",
            "The compatible floor remains OpenCode 1.16.2; 1.18.10 is the latest source-reviewed release and the exclusive 1.18.11 ceiling blocks unreviewed releases. This is compatibility, not certification; macOS last_validated_version remains empty pending a durable green latest-version run.",
            "OpenCode 1.18.10 declares permission.ask in plugin types but does not dispatch it in the tagged runtime; permission.asked/replied are observe-only events, so native ask remains false."
